data: {"sections":[{"section_id":"cause_title","type":"template","content":"IN THE HIGH COURT OF JHARKHAND AT RANCHI\n\nCr. Misc. No. _____ of 2026\n\nIN THE MATTER OF:\n\nRajesh Mahto\nS/o Late Shri Dhananjay Mahto\nAge: 42 years\nR/o Flat 3A, Ashok Nagar, Main Road, Ranchi - 834002\n                                              ... Petitioner\n\nVersus\n\nState of Jharkhand through the Principal Secretary, Home Department, Government of Jharkhand, Ranchi\n                                              ... Respondent","alignment":"center"},{"section_id":"application_heading","type":"template","content":"APPLICATION FOR ANTICIPATORY BAIL UNDER SECTION 482 OF THE BHARATIYA NAGARIK SURAKSHA SANHITA, 2023","alignment":"center"},{"section_id":"addressing_clause","type":"template","content":"TO,\nTHE HONOURABLE HIGH COURT OF JHARKHAND AT RANCHI,\nRanchi\n\nMOST RESPECTFULLY SHOWETH:","alignment":"left"},{"section_id":"body","type":"ai_generated","content":"1. That the applicant apprehends arrest in connection with FIR No. 142/2026 dated 18.04.2026, registered at PS Doranda, under Sections BNS 318(4), BNS 336(3) of BNS, 2023. The applicant has NOT been arrested yet but genuinely apprehends arrest and detention by the police authorities in the said case and hence seeks protection of anticipatory bail from this Hon'ble Court under Section 482 of BNSS, 2023.\n\n2. That the applicant apprehends arrest in connection with FIR No. 142/2026 dated 18.04.2026 lodged at PS Doranda, Ranchi. The said FIR has been lodged on the basis of a false and frivolous complaint by the de-facto complainant arising out of a commercial partnership dispute involving a transport business.\n\n3. That the applicant is a well-known transporter in Ranchi and has been engaged in legitimate transport business for several years. The present case is nothing but a result of a civil commercial dispute between business partners which has been given a criminal colour by the complainant to harass and humiliate the applicant.\n\n4. That the applicant undertakes to cooperate fully with the investigation and not to leave the territorial jurisdiction of Jharkhand without prior permission of this Hon'ble Court. The applicant is always available for interrogation and has never avoided any legal process.\n\n5. That the applicant has been falsely implicated in the present case due to malicious intent of the complainant. The allegations levelled against the applicant are completely false, frivolous and without any basis. The complainant has lodged the present FIR with ulterior motives to settle scores arising out of their commercial partnership dispute.\n\n6. That the dispute between the applicant and the complainant is purely civil in nature pertaining to their transport business partnership and the same does not involve any criminal liability. The complainant has deliberately given criminal colour to a purely civil commercial dispute to pressurize the applicant.\n\n7. That the applicant is a respectable citizen with no criminal antecedents and has never been involved in any criminal case earlier. The applicant has deep roots in the community and is well-known in business circles of Ranchi for his integrity and honest dealings.\n\n8. That custodial interrogation of the applicant is not necessary as the applicant is willing to join the investigation as and when required by the investigating agency. The applicant undertakes to cooperate fully with the investigation and shall not hamper the same in any manner.\n\n9. That the fundamental right to life and liberty as enshrined under Article 21 of the Constitution of India cannot be curtailed arbitrarily. The Hon'ble Supreme Court in the case of Sushila Aggarwal v. State (2020) 5 SCC 1 has laid down the conditions for granting anticipatory bail and emphasized that personal liberty is a precious right which should not be lightly interfered with.\n\n10. That the applicant has deep roots in the community and is engaged in legitimate business activities. There is no possibility of the applicant fleeing from justice or tampering with evidence. The applicant has always been law-abiding and has never avoided any legal process.\n\n11. That the investigation in the present case is pending and the applicant apprehends that he may be arrested and harassed by the police authorities. Grant of anticipatory bail will ensure that the applicant's constitutional rights are protected while ensuring his availability for investigation.\n\n12. That in the interest of justice and to protect the fundamental rights of the applicant, this Hon'ble Court may be pleased to grant anticipatory bail to the applicant with such conditions as this Hon'ble Court may deem fit and proper."},{"section_id":"prayer","type":"template","content":"PRAYER\n\nIt is, therefore, most humbly prayed that this Hon'ble Court may graciously be pleased to:\n\na) Grant Anticipatory Bail to the Petitioner, Rajesh Mahto, in the event of arrest in connection with FIR No. 142/2026 dated 18.04.2026, PS Doranda, under Section 482 of BNSS, 2023, on such terms and conditions as this Hon'ble Court may deem fit;\n\nb) Direct that in the event of arrest, the Petitioner shall be released on bail forthwith;\n\nc) Pass such other orders as this Hon'ble Court may deem fit and proper in the facts and circumstances of the case, in the interest of justice.\n\nAnd for this act of kindness, the petitioner shall ever pray.","alignment":"left"},{"section_id":"verification","type":"template","content":"VERIFICATION\n\nI, Rajesh Mahto, the Petitioner herein above named, do hereby solemnly affirm and state that the contents of paragraphs 1 to 12 of the above petition are true and correct to the best of my knowledge and belief and nothing material has been concealed therefrom.\n\nVerified at Ranchi on this _____ day of _________, 2026.\n\nDEPONENT\n\n\n_________________________\nRajesh Mahto\n(Petitioner)","alignment":"left"},{"section_id":"advocate_block","type":"template","content":"THROUGH:\n\n_________________________\nSmoke Test\nAdvocate\nEnrollment No. ____________________\n\nPlace: Ranchi\nDate: 06 May 2026","alignment":"right"},{"section_id":"disclaimer","type":"template","content":"AI-assisted draft — verify with applicable law before filing. Lawie does not provide legal advice.","alignment":"center","style":"footer_small_gray"}]}

